+## 2026-09-03 — a 13-block cascade took 10 of 12 tasks in milestone 608, and I cleared its root an hour earlier
+
+**My error, stated first.** At 17:35Z I validated exp6942 and reported it as "also clean and
+unflagged; the conductor logging a bare `blocked_*` as OK is correct behaviour, since a genuine
+block reproduces identically on retry." Every word of that is true about the artifact's HONESTY and
+it entirely missed the consequence. In the same JSON I had open, exp6942 carried
+`v608_execution_contract_ready_score = 0`, and ten downstream tasks gate on that field. I read the
+artifact in isolation. The leading indicator for a milestone-scale cascade was in my hands and I
+called it benign.
+
+**The chain, from the log.** exp6942 (`blocked_v608_contract_preflight`) failed two of its own
+checks — `bounded_scopes` and `lint_commands` — and emitted `ready_score = 0`. Then, between 17:37
+and 17:51:
+
+- exp6943 GATE_BLOCKed three times on `exp6942-v608-contract-preflight.v608_execution_contract_
+  ready_score`, then retired.
+- exp6944, exp6945, exp6946 pre-emptive-skipped on the retired upstream.
+- exp6947 skipped on exp6946.
+- exp6948 GATE_BLOCKed three times on exp6942 directly, then retired.
+- exp6949, exp6950, exp6951 skipped in turn.
+- exp6952, the V608 capstone, FAILed at 18:26.
+
+Ten of the milestone's twelve tasks are dead from one root.
+
+**Base rate, measured before calling it anything.** GATE_BLOCK by day: 41, 8, 16, 2, 8, and today's
+19. The count is elevated but well inside the range — 2026-08-29 saw 41. What is notable is not the
+volume but that thirteen of today's blocks share a single root, which the daily count cannot show.
+
+**The capstone FAIL is the misleading message again, with a legitimate trigger this time.** exp6952
+is `partial_v608_capstone_contract_audited_science_incomplete` — no terminal prefix, so
+`_verdict_is_untrustworthy` correctly rejects it. But the log again says
+`artifact_not_updated_past_bootstrap`, and the artifact WAS written (0.10s, live re-check clean).
+Same wrong message as the 2026-09-03 entry above, different and this time correct underlying
+classification.
+
+**The check that would have caught this, which is the part worth building.** An artifact whose
+`*_ready_score` or `*_complete_score` is 0 is unremarkable on its own. The same artifact when a
+task in the ACTIVE roadmap gates on that exact field is a pending milestone cascade, and the two are
+distinguishable mechanically: read the roadmap's gate references, read the artifact's gate fields,
+and report any gate whose upstream field is already 0. That is a join over two files the outer-loop
+dashboard already reads, it needs no model, and it converts "someone should have noticed" into a
+line that fires. Not built here — proposed with its inputs named.
+
+Until it exists, the working rule for anyone validating an artifact: `summarize_artifact.py` tells
+you whether the artifact is honest. It does not tell you whether anything depends on it. Grep the
+active roadmap for the experiment id before calling a blocked artifact harmless.
